WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.740
If you have ever taken a trip to Suntop Mountain
in the Mount Baker-Snoqualmie National Forest,

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:11.440
Washington State, then you may have come across
an old wooden structure - The Suntop Fire

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:12.620
Lookout.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:17.300
Built in the early 1930s, the building was
used by the US Forest Service to keep watch

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.570
for any fires in the nearby woodland.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:26.070
At one point, Suntop Fire Lookout would have
been manned 365 days a year, complete with

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:29.470
a bed for staff who were stationed there on
rotation.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:34.310
The single story lookout house overlooks the
scenic valleys of the White River and Huckleberry

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:38.480
Creek, but you’re not here for an informative
tourist guide.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:42.900
You probably don’t care about the frankly
fascinating history of the lookout and how

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:48.240
it was used as part of the Aircraft Warning
Service during World War 2, watching for enemy

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.240
planes.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:55.770
No, you’re here because something much darker
lurks inside the Suntop Fire Lookout.

00:00:55.770 --> 00:01:01.590
And even though it appears to be a simple,
one-story-tall wooden structure, it certainly

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.439
is not short on space.

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:10.970
SCP-3333 refers to an anomaly that the Foundation
discovered inside the Suntop Fire Lookout

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:11.970
house.

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:16.670
The building’s interior is a single, square
room, measuring fourteen feet by fourteen

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:20.799
feet, with large windows on all four sides.

00:01:20.799 --> 00:01:25.600
When standing inside Suntop Fire Lookout,
looking up at the wooden ceiling, one will

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.890
immediately notice a trapdoor.

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:29.040
No big deal, right?

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.710
A lot of places have a ceiling entrance to
a small crawl space, there is probably nothing

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:37.229
behind the trapdoor, apart from a dusty, old
attic.

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:41.869
There’s a latch that maybe once had a padlock
there, but not anymore.

00:01:41.869 --> 00:01:45.439
Opening the trapdoor will reveal a collapsible
ladder.

00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:50.139
Should anyone be brave, or indeed foolish
enough, to begin to climb, then they’ll

00:01:50.139 --> 00:01:56.119
soon find themselves right back where they
started, inside Suntop Fire Lookout.

00:01:56.119 --> 00:01:58.380
Or so it will seem.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.510
The thing about being in a place like the
Mount Baker-Snoqualmie National Forest that

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:07.770
surrounds Suntop Fire Lookout is that woodland
areas are teeming with life.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:12.189
Not just plants and trees, but birds and other
animals of the forest.

00:02:12.189 --> 00:02:17.439
You can never truly be alone in a setting
like that, there is always life everywhere

00:02:17.439 --> 00:02:18.510
around you.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:23.810
So, when you ascend the ladder, and climb
out right back into the Suntop Fire Lookout,

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:27.489
that is the first, most noticeable difference
you will find.

00:02:27.489 --> 00:02:33.069
It may take a while at first, but the nagging
absence of something usually so abundant in

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:35.700
a forest will eventually become obvious.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:39.230
It’s quiet, far too quiet.

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:43.629
No birdsong, or the sound of distant calls
from woodland critters.

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:46.990
Just silence, all around.

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:52.220
Anyone ascending the ladder will find themselves
in a copy of Suntop Fire Lookout’s interior,

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:56.409
one story higher than the ground level of
the small wooden building, with the stairs

00:02:56.409 --> 00:03:01.579
leading up to the front door getting taller
each time to reach up to the higher and higher

00:03:01.579 --> 00:03:02.579
building.

00:03:02.579 --> 00:03:08.130
Now, you know the SCP Foundation and the types
of bizarre, inter dimensional anomalies they’re

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:09.659
used to dealing with.

00:03:09.659 --> 00:03:15.360
Perhaps SCP-3333 is a mirror dimension, or
a plane of existence where sound doesn’t

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:16.360
travel.

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:20.579
It certainly seems to be identical to the
Suntop Fire Lookout, save for the lack of

00:03:20.579 --> 00:03:22.880
any organic life outside.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:29.609
Of course, it’s what you’ll find living
inside SCP-3333 that you may want to worry

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:30.799
about.

00:03:30.799 --> 00:03:35.269
Climbing higher, up the next ladder and through
the next trapdoor, every time with the same

00:03:35.269 --> 00:03:36.269
result.

00:03:36.269 --> 00:03:41.299
You appear at another copy of Suntop Fire
Lookout, each one higher up than the last.

00:03:41.299 --> 00:03:46.629
What first seemed to be an innocuous, unassuming
wooden building is now an endless ascension

00:03:46.629 --> 00:03:52.940
up into the heavens, towards the unknown in
silence, without a shred of plant or animal

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:54.599
life outside.

00:03:54.599 --> 00:03:58.689
As you climb, perhaps you start to think how
much higher these copies go.

00:03:58.689 --> 00:04:02.670
This might even be the biblical Jacob’s
Ladder, connecting Heaven and Earth.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:04.630
That would be nice, wouldn’t it?

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:09.269
If you were gradually climbing your way up
to paradise, it might make it worth the trip.

00:04:09.269 --> 00:04:13.019
But SCP-3333 is nothing that pleasant.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:16.060
You wouldn’t be the first to attempt this
long climb.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:22.900
When the SCP Foundation first discovered SCP-3333,
a research detail set up an onsite base camp

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:25.450
to examine this spatial anomaly.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:31.759
Their first exploration involved sending a
member of D-class personnel, designated D-4f68a,

00:04:31.759 --> 00:04:32.759
up the ladder.

00:04:32.759 --> 00:04:38.340
His D-number is a hexadecimal code that, when
translated to text, reads ‘Oh’, so we’ll

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.639
call him that for brevity’s sake.

00:04:40.639 --> 00:04:48.350
During the first day’s exploration, Oh was
able to climb 184 iterations of SCP-3333,

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:51.400
communicating with head researcher Doctor
Williams below.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:57.020
On the second day, Oh could see a pair of
figures standing motionless on a nearby ridge,

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:02.130
but the pair could not be seen by Doctor Williams
and the other researchers at the base camp.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:07.069
Both figures disappeared shortly after Oh
spotted them with the camera he had been issued,

00:05:07.069 --> 00:05:11.680
and he felt uneasy, almost certain that he
saw them point at him.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:18.340
The next day, at the 345th copy of Suntop
Fire Lookout, Oh’s behavior started to noticeably

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:19.340
change.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:23.880
Previously, he had been anxious about the
long climb, and hadn’t questioned directions

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.759
given to him by Doctor Williams.

00:05:25.759 --> 00:05:31.670
Now, he seemed to speak more casually, resisting
instructions, asking Williams to climb back

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:35.099
down and even calling her ‘Doc’ instead
of ‘Doctor’.

00:05:35.099 --> 00:05:40.740
Oh also reported seeing writing on the walls,
but there was no evidence of this on his camera.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:44.349
It appeared that something had started to
affect him.

00:05:44.349 --> 00:05:50.160
It was when Oh reached level 527 that things
seemed to change more dramatically.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:56.879
Rather than SCP-3333 continuing upwards, the
copies of Suntop Fire Lookout no longer had

00:05:56.879 --> 00:05:59.129
a trapdoor or ladder.

00:05:59.129 --> 00:06:03.580
They seemed to be arranged side by side, in
a grid-like pattern.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:08.410
Stepping out of the main doorway, Oh remarked
on the lack of sunlight, and a walkway that

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:13.879
connected directly to the front door of the
next iteration of SCP-3333.

00:06:13.879 --> 00:06:20.259
Oh complained about the lack of natural light,
and again requested to be allowed back down.

00:06:20.259 --> 00:06:25.419
Doctor Williams instructed Oh to use the flashlights
he was provided, but they wouldn’t activate

00:06:25.419 --> 00:06:27.509
and their spare batteries had vanished.

00:06:27.509 --> 00:06:33.259
Oh then noticed a sudden movement, and just
then his microphone and camera feed went dead,

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:36.320
almost as if someone had turned them off.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:41.289
It appeared that SCP-3333 had something else
lurking up there.

00:06:41.289 --> 00:06:46.370
Doctor Williams oversaw the second expedition
into SCP-3333.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:51.550
This time members of Mobile Task Force Mod-0,
also known by the codename “Characteristic

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:54.180
Eigenspaces”, were sent up the ladder.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:58.449
Their ascent through the various copies of
Suntop Fire Lookout were not as eventful as

00:06:58.449 --> 00:07:03.750
Oh’s, with no signs of mysterious figures,
or anxious feelings that Oh seemed to feel

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:05.120
as he climbed.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:10.210
When they reached level 527, where the copies
of the lookout stop progressing upwards and

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:15.310
spread out in a pattern instead, their lights
and equipment all seemed to be in working

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:16.310
order.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:21.659
However, as the MTF team split up, one by
one they encountered some sort of anomaly,

00:07:21.659 --> 00:07:27.580
or an effect of SCP-3333 that caused each
of them to vanish into the dark.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:31.370
Either that, or something took them.

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:37.180
These MTF units reappeared confused, and Mod-5,
the team’s leader, Graham Purcell, issued

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:42.440
an order to retreat and the entire squad went
back down the ladders for several days until

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:45.289
they finally reached the base camp again.

00:07:45.289 --> 00:07:51.039
The members of Mod-0 were adamant they did
not wish to climb SCP-3333 again, but Doctor

00:07:51.039 --> 00:07:55.039
Williams was beginning to understand more
of the anomaly’s effects.

00:07:55.039 --> 00:08:00.410
It appeared to cause abrupt changes to people’s
personalities, along with some sort of phenomenon

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:04.750
that caused things to appear and disappear
the higher one climbed.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:09.340
Assuming these were the results of a memetic
effect, Doctor Williams dispatched a ‘counter

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:11.800
memetics specialist’ for the next expedition.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:17.099
This specialist was a blind, deaf, and mute
woman known as Annette or the ‘Nullwalker’,

00:08:17.099 --> 00:08:22.610
who communicated via a signaling system embedded
in her hand, but was otherwise immune to any

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:25.020
memetic influences.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:29.030
Observed by Doctor Williams and Graham Purcell
at base camp, Annette made her way to the

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:35.329
top of SCP-3333, reporting that she was aware
of someone watching her from outside the copies

00:08:35.329 --> 00:08:37.690
of Suntop Fire Lookout.

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:42.700
On her body camera, a flicker of motion occurred,
something looking through the windows that

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:46.149
ducked out of frame when the camera passed
in its direction.

00:08:46.149 --> 00:08:52.170
At the apex of SCP-3333, Annette kept her
flashlight off, but reported that she could

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:56.570
detect blood, following it to what she assumed
was a body.

00:08:56.570 --> 00:09:01.079
Sounds of movement surrounded her, and as
Annette switched on her flashlight, Williams

00:09:01.079 --> 00:09:04.851
and Purcell saw that it wasn’t a body in
front of her.

00:09:04.851 --> 00:09:10.440
Instead, it was a pile of rotting organs,
decomposing muscles and discarded bones.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:18.170
And among the pile was a metal dog tag, that
read ‘MTF Mod-5: Graham Purcell’; the

00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:22.110
same man who was sitting next to Doctor Williams
at base camp.

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:25.950
Well, the same man on the outside at least.

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:32.839
The explanation for everything going on inside
SCP-3333, all these strange occurrences and

00:09:32.839 --> 00:09:37.850
disappearances, finally came in a video sent
from Doctor Williams’ cell phone.

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:43.550
In it, a panicked Williams, covered in blood,
was fleeing from something at the top of the

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:46.070
recursive stack of SCP-3333.

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:52.670
There was no memetic effect at the apex of
the Suntop Fire Lookout copies.

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:57.800
Nothing was causing the people that the Foundation
sent up to act unlike themselves.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:01.310
They simply weren’t themselves anymore.

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:05.570
According to her frantic video, Doctor Williams
had discovered the truth about what else was

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:08.630
hiding within SCP-3333.

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:12.750
With just the right amount of vagueness and
intrigue, the research team had been drawn

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:13.750
in.

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:18.470
It was as if they’d been lured in by the
lights of an anglerfish, realizing their grim

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:20.980
fate only too late.

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:25.690
The D-class ‘Oh’, the MTF team, even Annette
had been replaced.

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:32.790
An unknown group of entities on the top level
of SCP-3333 had been carefully observing them,

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:38.040
waiting until they would not be seen to slip
in and switch places.

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:43.130
These entities had been creating imagined
anomalous effects, like Oh seeing figures

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:48.340
that weren’t really there, as a way of luring
more bodies further up the stack.

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:54.990
They wanted the Foundation to keep sending
expeditions into SCP-3333, to keep them coming

00:10:54.990 --> 00:10:56.100
back.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:11:01.300
The mass of organs, musculature, and bones
that Annette had stumbled across, revealing

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:06.959
the ruse, had once belonged to Graham Purcell,
before he was replaced.

00:11:06.959 --> 00:11:12.260
You see, the entities residing in SCP-3333
weren’t just copying people.

00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:18.050
They weren’t possessing them or mind-controlling
them, or even shape shifting to steal a person’s

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:19.050
likeness.

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:21.290
They were taking skin.

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:27.180
These creatures hollowed out Graham, Oh, Annette
and the MTF team, pulling out their innards

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:32.639
and crawling their way inside, filling these
fleshy puppets and leaving their internal

00:11:32.639 --> 00:11:34.639
organs to rot.

00:11:34.639 --> 00:11:40.459
These hollowed out people become vessels for
the entities of SCP-3333 to hide in.

00:11:40.459 --> 00:11:48.380
The whole thing had been a trap, intentionally
exploiting human weaknesses, intrigue, unanswered

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:49.740
questions.

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:54.680
You know what they say about curiosity, and
these entities used it to bring more potential

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:58.320
vessels to the top of SCP-3333.

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:03.339
They pretended to be the people who they had
replaced, imitating them so the Foundation

00:12:03.339 --> 00:12:08.810
would send more personnel to explore the tower,
increasing their supply of skins.

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:16.190
Graham’s dog tag had revealed the deception,
and Doctor Williams had escaped up SCP-3333.

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:20.300
The members of the research team that had
already been replaced were hot on her tail,

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:26.860
determined to catch and hollow her out too,
and by the end of her video, they had succeeded.

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:32.089
A month later though, a team delivering supplies
realized what had happened and the trapdoor

00:12:32.089 --> 00:12:33.270
was sealed.

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:38.199
Suntop Fire Lookout was put under permanent
guard, but at least fifty personnel were killed

00:12:38.199 --> 00:12:40.529
or replaced by one of the entities.

00:12:40.529 --> 00:12:46.290
A new Mobile Task Force, Lamda-1 “Maxwell’s
Demons” was created to hunt down and neutralize

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:52.269
any of the entities that escaped SCP-3333,
but it’s still unknown how many left the

00:12:52.269 --> 00:12:58.510
tower and are still out there somewhere, waiting
to use someone’s curiosity about the strange

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:01.070
and unknown against them.

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:07.680
Now check out “SCP-1861 - The Crew of the
HMS Wintersheimer” and “SCP-3999 - I Am

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:12.540
At The Center of Everything That Happens To
Me” for more tales of anomalous terror from

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:13.639
SCP Explained!

